M and L differ from the libraries in one place only: in signal() the table
index is computed in BX (sig kept in SI) where the libraries compute it in
SI; every other byte matches.  No source form tried changes this register
choice; the library may have been built with a slightly different compiler
revision.  The S and C objects are the same source compiled /ms and /mc.
